WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.601 --> 00:00:03.469
-President Trump was swept
into office

00:00:03.469 --> 00:00:06.572
in part because of his
supposed blue collar appeal.

00:00:06.572 --> 00:00:09.409
For example, he promised
that America's truckers

00:00:09.409 --> 00:00:11.444
would prosper
under his administration.

00:00:11.444 --> 00:00:13.880
So how are they doing after
three years under Trump?

00:00:13.880 --> 00:00:17.216
This is "The Check In."
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:17.216 --> 00:00:19.585
[ Bell dings ]

00:00:19.585 --> 00:00:21.587
Trucking is a huge American
industry,

00:00:21.587 --> 00:00:23.256
worth over $700 billion

00:00:23.256 --> 00:00:25.424
and employing over 7 million
Americans,

00:00:25.424 --> 00:00:28.094
which is why Trump pandered
so hard during an event

00:00:28.094 --> 00:00:29.962
with trucking industry
executives

00:00:29.962 --> 00:00:31.297
at the White House
a few years ago

00:00:31.297 --> 00:00:33.599
when he donned
an "I love trucks" button

00:00:33.599 --> 00:00:35.568
and then played inside of one.

00:00:35.568 --> 00:00:38.071
[ Crowd applauds ]

00:00:38.071 --> 00:00:40.573
[ Laughter ]

00:00:40.573 --> 00:00:43.076
[ Honking ]

00:00:43.076 --> 00:00:45.411
-Tell me how to get out of here.

00:00:45.411 --> 00:00:46.646
[ Laughter ]

00:00:46.646 --> 00:00:49.048
-Nothing says
"I'm a real blue-collar guy"

00:00:49.048 --> 00:00:51.551
like "How do you get me
down from a truck?"

00:00:51.551 --> 00:00:52.885
[ Laughter ]

00:00:52.885 --> 00:00:54.554
This looks like
a geriatric remake

00:00:54.554 --> 00:00:55.855
of "Smokey and the Bandit."

00:00:55.855 --> 00:00:58.290
"Wait for me, Bandit.
Snowman's gotta pee again.

00:00:58.290 --> 00:01:00.126
10-4."
[ Laughter ]

00:01:00.126 --> 00:01:02.895
When Trump later addressed
trucking CEOs and executives

00:01:02.895 --> 00:01:05.998
at the White House, even he had
to admit that he was full of it.

00:01:05.998 --> 00:01:08.567
-Through day and night
and all kinds of weather,

00:01:08.567 --> 00:01:12.104
truckers course the arteries
of our nation's highways.

00:01:12.104 --> 00:01:14.007
You carry anything
and everything,

00:01:14.007 --> 00:01:16.576
the food that stocks
our shelves,

00:01:16.576 --> 00:01:18.912
the fuel that runs our cars,

00:01:18.912 --> 00:01:21.781
and the steel that
builds our cities.

00:01:21.781 --> 00:01:23.983
You think I wrote that?
It's not bad.

00:01:23.983 --> 00:01:27.153
[ Laughter ]

00:01:27.153 --> 00:01:29.789
Save that.
I want to save that paragraph.

00:01:29.789 --> 00:01:32.759
-No one thinks you wrote that.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:32.759 --> 00:01:36.863
You read that like a kid
reciting a poem in class.

00:01:36.863 --> 00:01:39.599
"Two roads diverged
in yellow wood."

00:01:39.599 --> 00:01:41.567
[ Laughter ]

00:01:41.567 --> 00:01:43.803
No one even thinks
you wrote this.

00:01:43.803 --> 00:01:46.038
[ Laughter ]

00:01:46.038 --> 00:01:47.907
Also, what did you mean
when you said,

00:01:47.907 --> 00:01:50.142
"I want to save that paragraph"?

00:01:50.142 --> 00:01:53.112
When will you ever have any
reason to use it again?

00:01:53.112 --> 00:01:54.280
[ Laughter ]

00:01:54.280 --> 00:01:56.282
"Happy Valentine's Day, Melania.

00:01:56.282 --> 00:01:58.251
You carry anything
and everything.

00:01:58.251 --> 00:02:01.253
The food that stocks
my shelves."

00:02:01.253 --> 00:02:03.756
Now, as Trump waxed poetic
about truck drivers

00:02:03.756 --> 00:02:05.425
and promised to
put American truckers first,

00:02:05.425 --> 00:02:07.126
drivers said he hasn't
delivered.

00:02:07.126 --> 00:02:09.028
In fact, the Trump
Administration has actually

00:02:09.028 --> 00:02:11.664
made things worse for many
truckers by enacting

00:02:11.664 --> 00:02:13.833
policies that hurt
them financially.

00:02:13.833 --> 00:02:16.435
Take Trump's tax law,
which he tried to sell

00:02:16.435 --> 00:02:20.373
as a huge tax break specifically
for truck drivers.

00:02:20.373 --> 00:02:22.374
And when he touted the plan in
front of hundreds of truckers

00:02:22.374 --> 00:02:23.609
and industry executives,

00:02:23.609 --> 00:02:25.244
it was the classic Trump
one-two punch --

00:02:25.244 --> 00:02:28.514
transparent pandering followed
by incoherent thoughts.

00:02:28.514 --> 00:02:30.916
-I want to tell you,
to the truckers in this room,

00:02:30.916 --> 00:02:32.785
which is a lot of people,

00:02:32.785 --> 00:02:34.087
you're going to make more money,

00:02:34.087 --> 00:02:36.088
you're going to do better
than ever before,

00:02:36.088 --> 00:02:39.926
more jobs, higher pay,
and lower taxes.

00:02:39.926 --> 00:02:42.828
This huge tax cut.

00:02:42.828 --> 00:02:47.000
[ Scattered booing ]

00:02:48.901 --> 00:02:51.037
Two words.
Huge and now rocket.

00:02:51.037 --> 00:02:53.539
Can you believe it?
I have 'em in the same --

00:02:53.539 --> 00:02:55.341
Rocket.

00:02:55.341 --> 00:02:56.975
You know what we're talking
about, folks.

00:02:56.975 --> 00:02:59.445
Don't worry about it.

00:02:59.445 --> 00:03:01.981
It will rocket fuel,

00:03:01.981 --> 00:03:05.885
and it will be rocket fuel
for our economy.

00:03:05.885 --> 00:03:08.921
-Now that I believe you wrote.

00:03:08.921 --> 00:03:11.924
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:11.924 --> 00:03:14.193
"It will be huge."

00:03:14.193 --> 00:03:16.128
[ Cheering ]

00:03:16.128 --> 00:03:19.799
"And then rocket fuel,

00:03:19.799 --> 00:03:23.135
and it will be...

00:03:23.135 --> 00:03:24.737
rocket fuel."

00:03:24.737 --> 00:03:27.940
[ Laughter ]

00:03:27.940 --> 00:03:29.275
So there you have it.

00:03:29.275 --> 00:03:31.844
Trump said truckers would
pay less and make more money

00:03:31.844 --> 00:03:33.846
than ever thanks
to his tax plan.

00:03:33.846 --> 00:03:35.748
So how did that go?

00:03:35.748 --> 00:03:37.883
-Do you feel like
this administration

00:03:37.883 --> 00:03:39.918
is listening to you as truckers?
-No, ma'am.

00:03:39.918 --> 00:03:42.287
-No, they're not listening,
not at all.

00:03:42.287 --> 00:03:45.390
-They say some of their issues
affect all Americans,

00:03:45.390 --> 00:03:48.094
like the Republican-led
tax bill.

00:03:48.094 --> 00:03:49.895
How many of you,
by a show of hands,

00:03:49.895 --> 00:03:51.931
saw your taxes increase
this year?

00:03:51.931 --> 00:03:53.265
-They all went up, yeah.

00:03:53.265 --> 00:03:55.267
-One, two.
-Yeah, this year they went up.

00:03:55.267 --> 00:03:56.736
-One, two -- all of you?

00:03:56.736 --> 00:03:59.938
So most of you saw
your taxes increase?

00:03:59.938 --> 00:04:02.641
The reason?
Something called a per diem.

00:04:02.641 --> 00:04:05.544
In the past, truckers could
deduct things like food

00:04:05.544 --> 00:04:08.680
and daily expenses
from their taxable income.

00:04:08.680 --> 00:04:12.251
Now, with Trump's new tax bill,
they no longer can.

00:04:12.251 --> 00:04:15.021
-I have a young family at home
and with our per diem,

00:04:15.021 --> 00:04:16.321
they took the per diem out.

00:04:16.321 --> 00:04:18.323
That made an $8,000 difference.

00:04:18.323 --> 00:04:20.426
-$8,000?
-What I personally paid.

00:04:20.426 --> 00:04:21.927
-So what were you paying
in taxes last year?

00:04:21.927 --> 00:04:23.463
-Nothing.
-Amazing.

00:04:23.463 --> 00:04:25.531
So while the tax plan
lowered rates

00:04:25.531 --> 00:04:27.033
for trucking industry executives

00:04:27.033 --> 00:04:28.868
who make millions of dollars
a year,

00:04:28.868 --> 00:04:30.403
it only made things worse
for those

00:04:30.403 --> 00:04:31.737
actually doing the driving.

00:04:31.737 --> 00:04:33.473
In fact, because of
Trump's tax law,

00:04:33.473 --> 00:04:36.008
accountants have had to tell
truck drivers that after years

00:04:36.008 --> 00:04:38.344
of being able to count on
receiving tax refunds,

00:04:38.344 --> 00:04:41.147
that they in fact would owe
thousands of dollars.

00:04:41.147 --> 00:04:43.883
As one small fleet owner put it,
they got screwed.

00:04:43.883 --> 00:04:46.519
It's so bad, a lot of them can't
even afford clothing

00:04:46.519 --> 00:04:48.588
for the women on their
mud flaps.

00:04:48.588 --> 00:04:53.559
[ Laughter ]

00:04:53.559 --> 00:04:55.561
And in this case, a lot
of the people getting screwed

00:04:55.561 --> 00:04:57.430
voted for Trump,
and they aren't just worse off

00:04:57.430 --> 00:04:58.764
because of his tax law.

00:04:58.764 --> 00:05:01.000
Truckers are also hurting
because of Trump's trade wars

00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:03.035
and tariffs, which, again,
is a direct contradiction

00:05:03.035 --> 00:05:04.470
to what he had promised.

00:05:04.470 --> 00:05:09.208
-America first means putting
American truckers first.

00:05:09.208 --> 00:05:12.445
When companies stay in America
and move to America,

00:05:12.445 --> 00:05:15.515
it's our wonderful workers
who reap the rewards,

00:05:15.515 --> 00:05:18.784
including our great truckers
who will have

00:05:18.784 --> 00:05:22.087
more products to deliver
and more contracts to fill.

00:05:22.087 --> 00:05:24.290
That's the way it happens.

00:05:24.290 --> 00:05:26.759
-Well, it turns out
that's not the way it happens.

00:05:26.759 --> 00:05:30.128
In fact, the exact opposite is
what ended up happening.

00:05:30.128 --> 00:05:33.398
-Industry data shows the rates
trucking companies charge

00:05:33.398 --> 00:05:36.902
are down nearly as much as 17%.

00:05:36.902 --> 00:05:40.005
The reason? In part,
the President's trade war.

00:05:40.005 --> 00:05:42.742
With fewer goods like steel
and electronics coming into

00:05:42.742 --> 00:05:45.845
U.S. ports, fewer trucks are
needed to move them.

00:05:45.845 --> 00:05:48.548
-These tariffs are having
real-life consequences

00:05:48.548 --> 00:05:51.851
on states that rely on,
for instance, trucking.

00:05:51.851 --> 00:05:54.887
These states, many of them voted
for President Trump.

00:05:54.887 --> 00:05:57.523
Some of America's biggest
trucking companies

00:05:57.523 --> 00:06:00.860
are blaming the U.S./China
trade war along with new tariffs

00:06:00.860 --> 00:06:02.728
for hurting their bottom line.

00:06:02.728 --> 00:06:04.396
-That's right.
Because of Trump's trade war,

00:06:04.396 --> 00:06:06.032
trucks have less to haul.

00:06:06.032 --> 00:06:07.967
But Trump would probably say,
"If you think about it,

00:06:07.967 --> 00:06:09.735
that means they can drive
smaller trucks

00:06:09.735 --> 00:06:12.138
and then it'll be easier
to get down from them."

00:06:12.138 --> 00:06:13.773
[ Laughter ]

00:06:13.773 --> 00:06:16.708
"Because they're very high
in the air."

00:06:16.708 --> 00:06:18.477
So Trump's tax law
and his trade wars have had

00:06:18.477 --> 00:06:19.979
a negative impact on truckers.

00:06:19.979 --> 00:06:22.214
In fact, one of the few policies
Trump enacted

00:06:22.214 --> 00:06:24.817
that trucking industry lobbyists
actually pushed for

00:06:24.817 --> 00:06:27.252
is one that arguably puts
everyone else on the road

00:06:27.252 --> 00:06:28.588
in danger.

00:06:28.588 --> 00:06:30.656
-The transportation department
is moving to relax

00:06:30.656 --> 00:06:32.658
federal regulations
on the number of hours

00:06:32.658 --> 00:06:34.393
that truckers can be
behind the wheel.

00:06:34.393 --> 00:06:37.763
-Highway safety advocates say
the contemplated changes

00:06:37.763 --> 00:06:40.399
would weaken the regulations
leading to driver fatigue,

00:06:40.399 --> 00:06:42.334
making roads
more dangerous.

00:06:42.334 --> 00:06:46.005
-They say truckers will put in
even longer days at a time

00:06:46.005 --> 00:06:49.809
when they say driver fatigue
is a serious problem.

00:06:49.809 --> 00:06:52.111
-For someone who loves trucks
so much, Trump doesn't seem

00:06:52.111 --> 00:06:54.513
to care much about the condition
of the person behind the wheel.

00:06:54.513 --> 00:06:56.982
Maybe he doesn't even realize
there are drivers.

00:06:56.982 --> 00:06:58.784
"I just assume the trucks
go all day

00:06:58.784 --> 00:07:00.953
and then at night
they turn back into giant robots

00:07:00.953 --> 00:07:03.623
and go to sleep."
[ Laughter ]

00:07:03.623 --> 00:07:06.225
So thanks to Trump's policies,
truckers are forced to work

00:07:06.225 --> 00:07:09.162
more for less pay in potentially
harmful conditions.

00:07:09.162 --> 00:07:11.830
And his ongoing trade wars could
put thousands of truck drivers

00:07:11.830 --> 00:07:13.232
out of work entirely.

00:07:13.232 --> 00:07:14.766
So the best we can hope
for is that truckers

00:07:14.766 --> 00:07:16.502
return the favor in 2020.

00:07:16.502 --> 00:07:18.037
This has been "The Check In."

00:07:18.037 --> 00:07:19.738
♪♪
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:19.738 --> 00:07:21.541
[ Bell dings ]

